# Intentionally empty.
#
# pnpm 11 reads ONLY auth and registry settings from .npmrc. Every other key is
# ignored silently — no warning, no error, and `pnpm config list` simply omits
# it. Settings placed here therefore LOOK enforced while doing nothing, which is
# exactly what happened to this file's supply-chain block (ignore-scripts,
# minimum-release-age=10080, save-exact, engine-strict, prefer-frozen-lockfile,
# audit-level) before 2026-08-03.
#
# Put pnpm settings in pnpm-workspace.yaml instead — see the hardening block
# there. Only add auth/registry keys to this file.
#
# Dropped rather than migrated:
#   prefer-frozen-lockfile — CI passes --frozen-lockfile explicitly
#   audit-level            — nothing runs `pnpm audit`
#   ignore-scripts         — pnpm 10+ blocks dependency build scripts by
#                            default; allowBuilds is the allowlist
